  "election_date": "2026-11-03",
  "description": "The 2026 election for Kansas's 4th Congressional District will be held on November 3, 2026, with the primary scheduled for August 4, 2026. The district covers 17 counties in southcentral Kansas, including Wichita, and has been represented by a Republican since 1994. Incumbent Republican Rep. Ron Estes, first elected in 2017, is seeking re-election and faces a primary challenge from Republican Frank McCollum. The Democratic primary features multiple contenders including retired Air Force Col. Chris Carmichael, attorney Katy Tyndell, and business manager Ryan Gilbert, while Drew Cranmer is running as the Libertarian nominee. The race is considered safely Republican by major election forecasters.",
